WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.380
Between Ghostbusters, Spaceballs, and Honey,
I Shrunk the Kids, Rick Moranis earned his

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.860
status as one of the great comedy icons of
the ‘80s. Sadly, the actor has since stepped

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.170
away from the camera, leaving us to wonder
exactly what happened. Here's what we know

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.470
about Rick Moranis leaving Hollywood, in his
own words.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:24.180
(Rick Moranis gibberish)

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.540
Family Man

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.400
Moranis stopped appearing in live-action movies
after his wife, Ann, died of breast cancer

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.289
in 1997. Immediately after, he shifted his
focus to raising their two children. In the

00:00:34.289 --> 00:00:38.329
rare interviews he's given over the years
since her passing, Moranis has remained nonchalant

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:42.820
about his decision to become a stay-at-home-dad.
In 2015, he told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:46.010
"I took a break, which turned into a longer
break.”

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:50.079
Fiercely protective of his children, he won't
even reveal their names to the press.

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:51.810
It’s Not Unusual

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:55.620
These days, giving up a multi-million-dollar
movie career at its peak might seem like a

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:59.739
crazy idea. But when he made his decision
to leave Hollywood, Moranis didn't think he

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:04.030
was doing anything out of the norm. He told
the podcast Bullseye with Jesse Thorn:

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:11.110
"Stuff happens to people every day, and they
make adjustments in their lives, for all kinds

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:21.320
of reasons. There was nothing unusual about
what happened or what I did."

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.350
In fact, Moranis believes people only paid
attention at the time because he was walking

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.070
away from money and fame.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:33.420
"Because I came from celebrity and fame and
what was a peak of a career, that was intriguing

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.900
to people. And to me it wasn't that, it wasn't
anything to do with that. It was just work,

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.369
and it was time to make an adjustment."

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:41.740
Missing the Action

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.680
Moranis described "a lot of sameness" when
it came to raising kids. So, he admitted to

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.350
Bullseye that there were certain parts about
acting that he did actually miss:

00:01:49.350 --> 00:02:01.100
"I missed the people, and I missed the very
refreshing nature of doing something radically

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.409
different every day."

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:06.590
Still, he didn't look back with any regrets.
He said later to The Hollywood Reporter:

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:11.290
"I found lots of joy and lots of rewards in
other places. I was working with really interesting

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:15.550
people, wonderful people. I went from that
to being at home with a couple of little kids,

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:19.540
which is a very different lifestyle. But it
was important to me. I have absolutely no

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.450
regrets whatsoever. My life is wonderful."

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.530
Don’t Call It A Comeback

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:29.390
Contrary to many reports, Moranis maintains
that he never actually retired from show business.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:33.020
Case in point: he's done a ton of voice work
over the years, including radio commercials

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.930
and Disney's Brother Bear film series.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:38.660
He’s also done some op-ed contributing for
The New York Times. So if you want to know

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.900
how many sinks he has, you’re in luck. Spoiler
alert: it’s five.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:47.060
Moranis has also released two albums over
ten years. The first, The Agoraphobic Cowboy,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:51.660
earned him a Grammy nomination for Best Comedy
Album. The second, My Mother's Brisket &amp; Other

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:56.900
Love Songs, hit stores in 2013. In other words,
he's totally still around. You just have to

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:58.239
listen more carefully.

00:02:58.239 --> 00:03:01.459
"Howdy I'm rick how are ya man?"

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:02.010
"Hello!"

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:06.670
"It's always swell to run across another oatmeal
fan."

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:07.489
All In Good Time

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:11.819
Naturally, when a star as big as Moranis takes
a break from making movies, the question's

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:16.220
going to come up. When will he be back? For
years, Moranis dodged that question, often

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:20.390
implying that acting just wasn't on his radar.
In 2006, he told USA Today:

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:24.599
"I'm a single parent, and I just found that
it was too difficult to manage raising my

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:29.170
kids and doing the traveling involved in making
movies. I found that I really didn't miss

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:32.980
it. In the last few years I've been offered
a number of parts in movies, and I've just

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.760
turned them down. I don't know whether I'll
go back to it or not."

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:40.629
However, in 2015, Moranis admitted to The
Hollywood Reporter that he's potentially interested

00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:44.890
in pursuing live-action roles in the future.
It's just going to have to be the right one,

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:45.370
saying:

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:49.400
"I still get the occasional query about a
film or television role and as soon as one

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.940
comes along that piques my interest, I'll
probably do it. I'm happy with the things

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:57.000
I said yes to, and I'm very happy with the
many things I've said no to. Yes, I am picky,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.330
and I'll continue to be picky. Picky has worked
for me."

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.930
Who You Gonna Call?

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:05.909
Paul Feig's much-anticipated Ghostbusters
reboot is among the many scripts that have

00:04:05.909 --> 00:04:09.680
come to Moranis over the years. Despite the
cameos from Bill Murray, Dan Aykroyd, and

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:14.700
Sigourney Weaver, Moranis turned the project
down. The reason? It didn’t appeal to him.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:15.920
He told The Hollywood Reporter:

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.549
"I wish them well. I hope it's terrific. But
it just makes no sense to me. Why would I

00:04:20.549 --> 00:04:24.169
do just one day of shooting on something I
did 30 years ago?"

00:04:24.169 --> 00:04:26.460
Fair enough, but we're still pretty bummed
he said no.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.189
